  "subtitle": "Gaussian elimination has two phases. Forward pass: use row operations to get 1s on the diagonal and 0s below it (upper triangular form). Back substitution: start from the bottom row where there's only one unknown, find it, then substitute upward until all unknowns are found.",
  "learningOutcome": "Gaussian elimination has two phases. Forward pass: use row operations to get 1s on the diagonal and 0s below it (upper triangular form). Back substitution: start from the bottom row where there's only one unknown, find it, then substitute upward until all unknowns are found.",
